WEBVTT

00:10.010 --> 00:13.840
<b>Incredible. Sarah’s creating
new signals every second.</b>

00:14.180 --> 00:15.840
<b>I want you to push her twice as hard.</b>

00:16.970 --> 00:19.350
<b>I don’t know if she can take
that kind of strain!</b>

00:19.810 --> 00:21.310
<b>I didn’t ask. Now do it.</b>

00:21.430 --> 00:22.270
<b>Yes sir.</b>

00:30.070 --> 00:32.110
<b>Her signal output’s multiplying!</b>

00:32.900 --> 00:36.490
<b>Makoto!</b>

00:37.660 --> 00:39.580
<b>CERN, where it all began.</b>

00:40.910 --> 00:45.710
<b>Six years ago, the secret Niantic Project
revealed the existence of XM.</b>

00:46.460 --> 00:47.290
<b>CERN...</b>

00:48.130 --> 00:49.960
<b>Sarah, is that where you are?</b>

00:55.180 --> 00:57.390
<b>"Truth." I assume that means yes.</b>

00:57.840 --> 00:59.600
<b>Sarah! Are you okay?</b>

01:00.060 --> 01:01.850
<b>Damn it! Can’t you hear?</b>

01:04.850 --> 01:05.770
<b>Sarah push through!</b>

01:06.230 --> 01:07.690
<b>Here goes nothing Makoto...</b>

01:08.190 --> 01:09.270
<b>and everything!</b>

01:13.360 --> 01:14.190
<b>What the...</b>

01:19.780 --> 01:20.910
<b>What’s this?</b>

01:21.870 --> 01:23.660
<b>Jack, do you know what this is all about?</b>

01:25.500 --> 01:26.330
<b>I got nothing.</b>

01:26.830 --> 01:28.920
<b>She must be trying to tell us something.</b>

01:35.800 --> 01:38.340
<b>Sarah’s stabilizing.
Output is off the charts.</b>

01:39.470 --> 01:43.180
<b>Incredible. Her abilities are beyond
what we thought was possible.</b>

01:46.940 --> 01:50.230
<b>Sarah... I need to understand
what you’re trying to say!</b>

01:55.990 --> 01:56.820
<b>Hey!</b>

01:58.910 --> 01:59.740
<b>What’re you doing?</b>

02:00.320 --> 02:01.280
<b>The only thing I can.</b>

02:02.450 --> 02:05.200
<b>What good will that do?
You just read memories, don’t you?</b>

02:05.290 --> 02:07.750
<b>It’s not about what I can do. It’s Sarah.</b>

02:20.800 --> 02:21.640
<b><i>Reach through!</i></b>

02:22.550 --> 02:23.390
<b><i>Open your mind!</i></b>

02:24.390 --> 02:25.270
<b>Makoto!</b>

02:26.720 --> 02:31.350
<b><i>Danger awaits</i>
<i>in the Portal Network, Agent.</i></b>

04:14.790 --> 04:15.710
<b>Where am I?</b>

04:16.710 --> 04:17.590
<b>Mornin’, sunshine.</b>

04:18.540 --> 04:19.880
<b>What happened?</b>

04:21.050 --> 04:22.050
<b>You don't remember?</b>

04:24.840 --> 04:25.930
<b>Okay then...</b>

04:33.140 --> 04:33.980
<b>Makoto!</b>

04:34.310 --> 04:35.140
<b>Sarah?!</b>

04:35.690 --> 04:38.230
<b>It worked. Can you hear me?</b>

04:39.150 --> 04:40.980
<b>I can. Are you okay?</b>

04:41.690 --> 04:44.150
<b>Not really. I’m far from okay.</b>

04:45.070 --> 04:48.070
<b>They're doing some experiments on me
using Dark XM.</b>

04:49.160 --> 04:51.830
<b>You have to fight back.
Nothing will stop us from saving you.</b>

04:52.580 --> 04:53.870
<b>Are you really talking to her?</b>

04:54.750 --> 04:57.080
<b>Makoto. Why is he with you?</b>

04:57.880 --> 04:59.670
<b>That’s a... pretty long story.</b>

05:01.460 --> 05:02.460
<b>His name’s Jack.</b>

05:03.260 --> 05:06.130
<b>We had a bit of a rocky start,
but he’s with us.</b>

05:06.800 --> 05:08.140
<b>Can she hear the both of us?</b>

05:08.680 --> 05:09.510
<b>Yes.</b>

05:09.850 --> 05:10.760
<b>She says she can.</b>

05:12.890 --> 05:14.520
<b>I need to ask you something, Sarah.</b>

05:16.100 --> 05:18.690
<b>My boss was Christopher Brandt.</b>

05:19.560 --> 05:21.020
<b>Have you met him or know him?</b>

05:23.190 --> 05:24.030
<b>She says no.</b>

05:24.610 --> 05:25.990
<b>Stop lying lie to me!</b>

05:26.070 --> 05:28.610
<b>He came to Hulong for you.
Gave himself up!</b>

05:28.990 --> 05:29.820
<b>I’m not lying.</b>

05:30.780 --> 05:33.830
<b>He said he came to Hulong to save me.
That’s all I know.</b>

05:35.160 --> 05:36.000
<b>And then...</b>

05:36.710 --> 05:38.500
<b><i>Destruction leads to creation.</i></b>

05:38.580 --> 05:41.040
<b><i>Remember that in the times to come.</i></b>

05:41.880 --> 05:43.090
<b>He went up in flames.</b>

05:43.760 --> 05:44.630
<b>Ridiculous!</b>

05:45.130 --> 05:50.140
<b>It looked like he just exploded.
Like the blast came from inside him.</b>

05:51.470 --> 05:54.020
<b>You’re saying he blew himself up?
Impossible.</b>

05:54.270 --> 05:56.390
<b>I saw it too when I touched Sarah’s ring.</b>

05:56.480 --> 05:59.310
<b>You expect me to believe that?!
It doesn’t make any sense!</b>

05:59.900 --> 06:02.690
<b>And how do you manage
to survive without a scratch?!</b>

06:02.770 --> 06:04.980
<b>Brandt must know the reason.</b>

06:05.440 --> 06:07.820
<b>Maybe it wasn’t just an ordinary explo--</b>

06:08.280 --> 06:09.160
<b>What’s wrong, kid?</b>

06:10.410 --> 06:11.240
<b>Makoto?!</b>

06:11.490 --> 06:13.080
<b>It hurts...</b>

06:15.040 --> 06:16.410
<b>You pushed yourself too hard.</b>

06:17.580 --> 06:18.410
<b>It’s too much for you</b>

06:19.580 --> 06:21.170
<b>-Sarah!
-What?</b>

06:21.250 --> 06:22.920
<b>Cut us off. He’s done.</b>

06:24.880 --> 06:27.880
<b>Sarah... We’re coming for you.</b>

06:42.310 --> 06:45.320
<b>I guess I blacked out after all that.</b>

06:46.190 --> 06:48.570
<b>What makes you so sure
that Sarah’s not lying to us?</b>

06:49.240 --> 06:52.950
<b>I just know. I told you.
I saw that same mem--</b>

06:53.030 --> 06:55.910
<b>I don’t care.
I don’t buy any of it from her.</b>

06:56.700 --> 06:57.700
<b>Or from you.</b>

07:05.290 --> 07:08.630
<b>Doesn’t matter, Jack!
Our goal’s still the same.</b>

07:10.010 --> 07:14.260
<b>We still have to find Sarah. Help her.
And put a stop to Hulong</b>

07:18.430 --> 07:21.560
<b>“Walk with me toward the truth
of this world.”</b>

07:25.440 --> 07:27.070
<b>Just something Brandt used to say a lot.</b>

07:28.940 --> 07:31.030
<b>You the head of the Brandt fanclub
or something?</b>

07:32.450 --> 07:35.490
<b>Christopher Brandt was unique.
Not like anyone else I’d ever met.</b>

07:37.790 --> 07:39.000
<b>It was four years ago...</b>

07:43.250 --> 07:46.710
<b>I was a mercenary.
Dodging bullets and chasing a paycheck.</b>

07:47.840 --> 07:51.300
<b>I didn’t know how my ability worked
back then, just that it did.</b>

07:53.380 --> 07:55.180
<b>That's when I met him.</b>

07:56.760 --> 07:58.810
<b>I’ve got a job for you,
if you’re interested.</b>

07:59.520 --> 08:04.190
<b>I'd like to use your power for protection.
How’s that for a change of pace?</b>

08:05.560 --> 08:06.810
<b>What do you want me to protect?</b>

08:09.110 --> 08:13.610
<b>I’m a scientist, you see.
Researching a new particle called XM.</b>

08:14.360 --> 08:15.200
<b>XM?</b>

08:16.280 --> 08:19.740
<b>It can influence the mind,
but it doesn’t dominate or control it.</b>

08:20.200 --> 08:22.460
<b>A sort of guidance, one could call it.</b>

08:24.420 --> 08:26.960
<b>It’s been very divisive, of course.</b>

08:27.710 --> 08:32.800
<b>Some see XM as salvation.
Wisdom and Enlightenment.</b>

08:33.510 --> 08:37.550
<b>Others resist it as a hostile force.
A takeover of the human mind.</b>

08:38.680 --> 08:43.430
<b>And then there are the nefarious
who see it as a path to power and profit.</b>

08:44.600 --> 08:50.860
<b>You’re in deep with zealots, rebels,
and others who don't like you.</b>

08:51.320 --> 08:52.780
<b>A sad truth, yes.</b>

08:54.700 --> 08:56.740
<b>But truths can always be changed.</b>

08:57.570 --> 09:01.490
<b>My research could guide humanity
toward a whole new way of being.</b>

09:02.910 --> 09:06.420
<b>An end to conflict, famine,
disease and discrimination.</b>

09:07.120 --> 09:09.380
<b>Imagine how humanity could advance.</b>

09:10.960 --> 09:15.510
<b>If that were just within our reach,
don’t you think it’d be worth protecting?</b>

09:17.890 --> 09:20.350
<b>At first, I figured he was
either naive or deluded.</b>

09:21.760 --> 09:23.930
<b>Living some utopian fantasy.</b>

09:25.390 --> 09:28.480
<b>My world was ugly.</b>

09:28.560 --> 09:30.770
<b>Full of death, pain and apathy.</b>

09:32.150 --> 09:35.820
<b>The way he laid out his vision
resonated with me.</b>

09:45.410 --> 09:46.250
<b>Damn!</b>

09:47.290 --> 09:48.250
<b>Brandt! Get away!</b>

09:50.250 --> 09:51.090
<b>Jack!</b>

09:53.880 --> 09:59.140
<b>It was the first time I’d used my ability
for a noble purpose.</b>

10:08.730 --> 10:10.730
<b>I’m still kicking, aren’t I?</b>

10:11.770 --> 10:16.110
<b>I thought I was going to lose you.
You gotta stop scaring me like that.</b>

10:16.780 --> 10:19.280
<b>Don’t give me that. I’m doing my job.</b>

10:20.410 --> 10:25.290
<b>And I’m doing mine. Protecting life.
In whatever way I can.</b>

10:26.580 --> 10:28.210
<b>I’m glad to have you back.</b>

10:34.960 --> 10:38.090
<b>You’re the reason I’m alive
and back here. I’m grateful.</b>

10:39.090 --> 10:40.720
<b>Are you going to continue your research?</b>

10:41.430 --> 10:43.720
<b>The research never stopped, my friend.</b>

10:44.930 --> 10:50.020
<b>We humans are a curious species.
We fight over mysterious things.</b>

10:51.100 --> 10:55.940
<b>I worry that if we can’t figure out
XM’s true nature soon enough,</b>

10:56.030 --> 10:59.530
<b>we’ll cross a point of no return.</b>

11:00.360 --> 11:04.530
<b>The true fabric of the universe
is right there in the XM.</b>

11:04.950 --> 11:07.410
<b>And it’s trying to show us
by guiding our minds.</b>

11:08.040 --> 11:13.500
<b>I believe XM can save us from
our insatiable desire of self-destruction.</b>

11:15.380 --> 11:18.670
<b>I refuse to stop
until I’ve accomplished that.</b>

11:19.590 --> 11:22.680
<b>It’s weird...
a scientist believing in destiny.</b>

11:27.430 --> 11:30.390
<b>If your vision can get us there,
we’ll be better for it.</b>

11:32.100 --> 11:34.440
<b>Lots of people will want you dead
because of it.</b>

11:38.320 --> 11:40.150
<b>So that’s why I’m gonna protect you.</b>

11:41.700 --> 11:43.360
<b>And this crazy dream of yours.</b>

11:48.330 --> 11:52.000
<b>He woke up something inside me
I thought was dead and gone.</b>

11:54.170 --> 11:57.130
<b>It sounds cheesy,
but he gave me a new life.</b>

11:58.840 --> 12:03.470
<b>The job was simply to protect him,
but it grew into something so much bigger.</b>

12:07.430 --> 12:10.140
<b>And then he tells me to watch after her.</b>

12:11.350 --> 12:14.980
<b>And so now,
I guess I’m just carrying that burden.</b>

12:15.980 --> 12:18.650
<b>And that’s why you’re still working
with me to find Sarah?</b>

12:20.690 --> 12:22.320
<b>You want to stop Hulong, don't you?</b>

12:27.450 --> 12:28.280
<b>Let’s give ‘em hell.</b>

13:06.990 --> 13:07.950
<b>That’s amazing.</b>

13:22.420 --> 13:23.260
<b>What now?</b>

13:23.630 --> 13:25.760
<b><i>Danger. Ambush. 200 meters.</i></b>

13:25.930 --> 13:26.760
<b>Jack! An ambush!</b>

13:34.770 --> 13:36.100
<b>Ouch...</b>

13:38.440 --> 13:39.310
<b>Move!</b>

13:39.400 --> 13:40.270
<b>Hold on!</b>

13:43.530 --> 13:45.320
<b>Dammit! Where are they shooting from?!</b>

13:46.490 --> 13:47.320
<b>There’s more?!</b>

13:47.610 --> 13:50.870
<b><i>The group surrounding you is not Hulong.</i></b>

13:51.530 --> 13:53.990
<b><i>They are not your enemies.</i>
<i>They may be able to help.</i></b>

13:54.080 --> 13:55.500
<b>What? Wait! Come back!</b>

14:00.460 --> 14:01.340
<b>Don’t move.</b>

14:14.470 --> 14:15.350
<b>Right here.</b>

14:15.980 --> 14:20.400
<b>She’s been transmitting these Glyphs.
Dozens of them during the experiment.</b>

14:21.480 --> 14:23.730
<b>This one is special.
It’s carrying a data wave.</b>

14:24.820 --> 14:28.360
<b>We sampled this signal
and reconstituted it as sound.</b>

14:29.150 --> 14:32.660
<b>She was communicating
with someone through the Portal Network.</b>

14:32.740 --> 14:34.580
<b>-Let me hear her.
-Of course.</b>

14:37.750 --> 14:41.630
<b>-Channelling speech through XM...
-Incredible, don’t you think?</b>

14:41.710 --> 14:46.090
<b>Are we assuming that whoever she
was transmitting to can decipher it?</b>

14:46.170 --> 14:48.050
<b>-Where is she?
-What?</b>

14:48.470 --> 14:50.550
<b>Where the hell is her damn portal?!</b>

14:51.300 --> 14:52.640
<b>I’ll get that for you right away.</b>

14:54.930 --> 14:56.180
<b>Here. The Portal’s here.</b>

14:57.350 --> 14:59.020
<b>Oh, I see.</b>

14:59.890 --> 15:01.230
<b>This worked out well.</b>

15:12.870 --> 15:14.870
<b>These guys aren’t Hulong?</b>

15:16.040 --> 15:17.830
<b>No. Take a look around.</b>

15:18.580 --> 15:21.580
<b>That emblem.
That’s the Enlightened eye.</b>

15:22.250 --> 15:23.710
<b>So they’re all on my side?</b>

15:25.090 --> 15:26.250
<b>This isn’t good.</b>

15:26.960 --> 15:27.800
<b>Jack?</b>

15:28.630 --> 15:29.920
<b>-Check them.
-Yes sir!</b>

15:39.930 --> 15:42.310
<b>Hey! What do you think you’re doing?!</b>

15:43.060 --> 15:45.900
<b>Jack’s never done anything to you!</b>

15:45.980 --> 15:47.070
<b>Stop, dammit!</b>

15:57.530 --> 15:58.950
<b>Do you have a deathwish?</b>

15:59.040 --> 15:59.870
<b>Wait!</b>

16:00.870 --> 16:03.120
<b>He’s Enlightened. He’s not a threat.</b>

16:04.710 --> 16:05.630
<b>I’m the enemy here!</b>

16:10.090 --> 16:11.300
<b>You make a good argument.</b>

16:14.430 --> 16:15.430
<b>Hold your fire!</b>

16:17.510 --> 16:20.850
<b>Weapons down, guys.
They aren’t your enemy.</b>

16:23.440 --> 16:24.650
<b>You their leader or something?</b>

16:26.230 --> 16:29.820
<b>I’ve managed to earn a bit of respect,
but that’s about it.</b>

16:30.530 --> 16:32.110
<b>Hank Johnson. Nice to meet ya.</b>

16:32.650 --> 16:33.490
<b>Johnson!</b>

16:33.780 --> 16:34.660
<b>You know him?</b>

16:35.030 --> 16:39.490
<b>He helped discover XM at Niantic.
Highly respected among the Enlightened.</b>

16:40.160 --> 16:42.200
<b>So what’s your story?</b>

16:42.290 --> 16:45.670
<b>Enlightened and Resistance, an odd pair.
What gives?</b>

16:49.420 --> 16:51.210
<b>Now I think I get the picture.</b>

16:52.090 --> 16:54.550
<b>You’re both on the warpath against Hulong.</b>

16:55.470 --> 16:57.720
<b>Your buddies almost put a stop to that.</b>

16:58.050 --> 17:00.350
<b>Sorry, but you kicked the hornet’s nest.</b>

17:01.390 --> 17:02.220
<b>What?</b>

17:02.810 --> 17:05.730
<b>They were protecting this place,
and you were armed.</b>

17:07.560 --> 17:08.400
<b>Tag along?</b>

17:14.700 --> 17:15.570
<b>You see that?</b>

17:17.610 --> 17:20.780
<b>That place is sacred to the Azmati tribe.</b>

17:21.950 --> 17:26.750
<b>Enter a conglomerate with Resistance ties.
They barge in and set up a mine.</b>

17:27.330 --> 17:28.290
<b>Sounds like Hulong.</b>

17:29.540 --> 17:33.340
<b>The Azmati tribe has protected
this land for generations.</b>

17:34.090 --> 17:39.140
<b>Their beliefs have a lot in common
with the Enlightened ideology of today.</b>

17:39.720 --> 17:40.930
<b>But with much more history.</b>

17:41.350 --> 17:43.060
<b>So those guys were Azmati.</b>

17:43.600 --> 17:48.480
<b>They tried to protect their holy grounds.
Fight back against the mine.</b>

17:49.190 --> 17:53.940
<b>But the conglomerate
brought in their mercs.</b>

17:54.610 --> 17:58.200
<b>A private military force
called Strategic Explorations, or SE.</b>

17:59.700 --> 18:02.490
<b>There’ve been casualties on both sides.</b>

18:02.580 --> 18:05.500
<b>Deepening the rift
between Resistance and Enlightened.</b>

18:06.040 --> 18:09.790
<b>Each new attack breeds
its own counterattack.</b>

18:10.710 --> 18:13.590
<b>So you can’t blame them
for not trusting the Resistance.</b>

18:14.710 --> 18:16.090
<b>That would explain it.</b>

18:16.170 --> 18:19.340
<b>And your fancy visor?
Raised some eyebrows.</b>

18:20.390 --> 18:22.890
<b>Why would the company choose
this place to build a mine?</b>

18:23.720 --> 18:26.230
<b>There’s a very special reason for that.</b>

18:26.980 --> 18:27.940
<b>See for yourself.</b>

18:33.110 --> 18:34.480
<b>Dark XM?!</b>

18:35.110 --> 18:37.570
<b>One of few Dark XM Portals on the planet.</b>

18:38.110 --> 18:44.030
<b>XM and Dark XM react with each other
to produce rare, highly valuable minerals.</b>

18:47.000 --> 18:49.500
<b>I found this in Japan.
Is this what you’re talking about?</b>

18:49.920 --> 18:52.960
<b>Sure is. That’s a Dark XM crystal.</b>

18:53.630 --> 18:54.460
<b>A crystal?</b>

18:54.960 --> 19:00.180
<b>Yeah. Something Hulong was working on
to stabilize Dark XM.</b>

19:00.260 --> 19:01.180
<b>What's it for?</b>

19:01.260 --> 19:04.100
<b>You name it. It could be applied
to any kind of technology.</b>

19:04.180 --> 19:08.520
<b>Every major institution in the world
is chasing this tech right now.</b>

19:14.310 --> 19:15.730
<b>Those are the SE's.</b>

19:16.400 --> 19:18.990
<b>It's dangerous to linger.
Let's head back to camp.</b>

19:22.530 --> 19:23.990
<b>I get their situation..</b>

19:24.370 --> 19:27.790
<b>But they have to realize
that Hulong is too big.</b>

19:28.540 --> 19:31.250
<b>The Azmati don't stand
a snowball’s chance in hell.</b>

19:32.250 --> 19:36.250
<b>If they know they’ll die, why fight?
What drives them?</b>

19:39.340 --> 19:40.760
<b>The Azmati have a legend.</b>

19:41.840 --> 19:45.390
<b>One they’ve passed down generations
since ancient times.</b>

19:47.310 --> 19:49.770
<b>“Those that die on sacred ground
will rise again and again...</b>

19:50.680 --> 19:54.230
<b>With flesh immortal,
their minds reshaped and reborn.”</b>

19:56.770 --> 20:01.950
<b>That legend gives them the courage
they need to fight. As for the truth...</b>

20:02.820 --> 20:05.660
<b>Those crystals aren’t the only use
for Dark XM.</b>

20:06.490 --> 20:09.450
<b>Under the right circumstances,
Dark XM could cause</b>

20:09.540 --> 20:12.160
<b>someone who has died to recurse.</b>

20:12.870 --> 20:13.710
<b>Recurse?</b>

20:14.540 --> 20:19.630
<b>The Dark XM forms a new being
that carries on the mind, body and soul.</b>

20:21.380 --> 20:24.840
<b>A Simulacrum.
A living person formed of XM.</b>

20:26.350 --> 20:30.020
<b>Recursion? Simulacrums? No! That’s crazy!</b>

20:30.640 --> 20:32.850
<b>I’m just telling you
what the Azmati believe in.</b>

20:34.770 --> 20:37.020
<b>Legends are thought vessels
that travel through time.</b>

20:37.730 --> 20:40.730
<b>Containing, every so often,
a grain of truth inside.</b>

20:47.660 --> 20:49.990
